# Per-run gate verdict logs + PR-verdict snapshots are runtime artifacts — not
# committed. The Conductor's close-out step may snapshot a run's records into its
# run report (.orchestration/_templates/run-report.md); the live log is local.
# (`*.json` added 2026-06-19 — the per-PR `PR-<N>-verdict.json` snapshots are
#  local-only like the `*.jsonl` gate logs; prevents stale-artifact dirty-tree
#  friction at the next run's readiness gate.)
# (`*.txt`/`*.graphql` added 2026-06-20 — scratch from gh GraphQL thread-resolve
#  steps during /pr-fix; same local-only runtime-artifact class.)
*.jsonl
*.json
*.txt
*.graphql

# Keep the directory, its schema doc, and the DURABLE verdict-log ledger tracked.
# gate-history.jsonl is the committed, cross-machine record the erosion alarm +
# promotion ledger read ("advance on data" needs the data to survive); the live
# gate-log.jsonl stays ignored. The snapshot step (orchestrate-gates.sh --gate
# snapshot) unions the live log into it at close-out.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!gate-history.jsonl
